WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.070
Speaker 1: Let's talk about Ron DeSantis.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:09.430
Let's talk about the 2024 primary, the biggest
signal yet that Ron DeSantis plans to run

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:15.880
for president in 2024, regardless of whether
Trump is a candidate, is that DeSantis is

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:21.520
now holding fundraisers with Republican mega-donors.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.689
And it's very clear what the plan is here.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.769
I mentioned this yesterday, and I said we
would delve into it more deeply today if the

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:35.260
Republican mega-donors say to de Santos, if
you run in 24, we will support you rather

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.760
than Trump.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:43.350
That gives DeSantis the confidence to go up
against Trump in a contested primary.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:48.660
One of the things that has infuriated Trump
about DeSantis is that over the last year,

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:57.810
when asked, Would you only run if Trump doesn't,
will you rule out a run if Trump does want

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.810
the nomination?

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:01.070
DeSantis has declined to make that promise.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.879
He's just said, I just haven't made a decision
yet.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:03.879
I haven't.

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:04.879
I haven't decided yet.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.329
And now DeSantis is doing a major fundraiser.

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:14.970
CNBC Reporting Florida Governor Ron DeSantis
Plans Utah Fundraiser with Republican Megadonor.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.689
Signaling possible presidential run.

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:20.000
Yeah, you you do that if you're thinking of
running for president.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.799
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis is planning
a private fundraiser in Utah with some of

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:26.870
the country's wealthiest Republican donors.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:32.600
DeSantis hasn't publicly ruled out a run for
president in 24, even if it means challenging

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.600
Trump.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.330
DeSantis spokeswoman Lindsay Cronut wouldn't
confirm any details, saying the campaign doesn't

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:44.820
discuss private fundraising events with members
of the press.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.579
This is going to be next week, the week of
July 18th.

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:54.079
Many of the attendees asked not to be identified
because the campaign is trying to keep the

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.439
private event from getting too much public
attention.

00:01:57.439 --> 00:02:04.670
The Santas is coming to Utah to raise money
for his 2022 gubernatorial reelection campaign.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:09.759
Fundraisers in far flung states like Utah,
more than 2000 miles from Florida, where this

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:15.629
is actually a candidate right now, often suggest
nature, national aspirations.

00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:19.680
So the next question is, what does the polling
look like?

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.319
DeSantis hasn't said he's running and Trump
hasn't said that he's running.

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:29.450
Well, we have recent data polling, Republican
primary polling, and it sort of looks okay

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.250
for Ron DeSantis considering he hasn't announced
anything yet.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.590
Polls on morning consult from a few days ago.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.690
Trump 52.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.920
DeSantis 21.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.370
Now understand.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.760
Trump's up throw.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.760
DeSantis is not a former president.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.140
DeSantis is not nearly as well-known as Trump,
not even not even marginally as well-known

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.409
as Trump.

00:02:52.409 --> 00:02:58.280
And DeSantis hasn't announced anything, and
he's already polling 21% from a few days prior.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:05.080
New York Times Siena College poll has DeSantis
with 25% against Trump plus 24 a few days

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.080
earlier.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:12.230
The courageous Conservatives PAC poll has
a lot of undecideds and other candidates,

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.659
but has Trump 38, DeSantis 17.

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:16.540
That's only a 21 point margin for DeSantis.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:21.280
And then a poll at the end of June as well
from Harvard University.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.610
Harris.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:28.909
DeSantis doing significantly better than Pence,
despite Pence being the former vice president.

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:30.680
So that's interesting.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:35.159
The polling numbers don't look bad for DeSantis,
despite the centers having taken no moves

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:36.159
yet.

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:40.920
And then maybe more importantly, at this early
stage, when you allow people to bet money

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.160
on who they believe will be the nominee.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.530
Sometimes you get more forward looking data
or information.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:53.610
And if you look at the betting markets right
now, there is only a seven cent difference.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.110
And I'll explain what that means between Donald
Trump and Ron DeSantis.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.689
This is not who will you support.

00:03:59.689 --> 00:04:02.220
This is BET money.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:07.920
Who will win the 2024 Republican presidential
nomination?

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:13.680
When it comes to Trump, you have to bet $0.42
to make a dollar.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.880
And when it comes to Ron DeSantis, you have
to bet $0.35 to make a dollar.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:25.400
That means it is seen as only slightly less
likely that DeSantis will be the nominee than

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.400
Trump.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:32.080
Those are incredible numbers this far out,
particularly considering that de Santos hasn't

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.080
announced anything.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.080
Now, Trump hasn't either.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.200
But as I said, Trump is much more well-known.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:43.970
And Donald Trump also is talking about running
in a way that that Ron DeSantis isn't also

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:44.970
relevant.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.200
Nobody else is even in the picture.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.270
I mean, you've got Nikki Haley Pence, Glenn
Youngkin, Mike Pompeo, Ted Cruz, Tim Scott,

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.460
just pennies, pennies, pennies on the dollar.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:58.750
So the truth is, if DeSantis wants this, it's
not a guarantee that he could win, but he

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.880
will be a player for sure.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.790
And if he gets that Republican mega-donor
support, if the Republican mega-donors kind

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:08.860
of give him the old wink wink and say, if
you were to run.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:12.960
We would be eager to support an alternative
to what we've done in the past.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.800
I think the Santos is very, very well positioned.

